<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Amundsen is a 55-year-old explorer with cold-induced neuropathic pain in the fingers of both hands after old frostbite, and an old fracture of the right upper arm, who comes for a preventive visit. He began duloxetine two weeks ago, 30 mg for a week and 60 mg for the past week, and still uses capsaicin cream on the worst fingers. He had mild nausea for the first few days, now gone, and no drowsiness. The finger pain is a little less in the milder spring weather. He trains with his floor springs, bathes in cold salt water every morning, and walks or skis most days. He sleeps about seven hours. He wants to bring his prevention up to date. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 55</td></tr><tr><td>Finger pain</td><td>A little less; duloxetine 60 mg for a week</td></tr><tr><td>Medicine effects</td><td>Mild nausea at first, now gone; no drowsiness</td></tr><tr><td>Activity</td><td>Strength training, cold baths, walking and skiing</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 1</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on paper in the waiting room and reviewed with him face to face by Dr. Solheim-Achebe. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, apart from his hands</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Worried about money; has friends nearby</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Rarely; a glass of wine at a dinner</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Strength training most mornings, walking and skiing</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Plain home cooking, fish several times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>No concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Cold-water bathing alone each morning; boats on the fjord; flies in small aircraft</td></tr><tr><td>Road safety</td><td>Drives; wears a seat belt</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent; slow with buttons and keys in the cold</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Long-standing near-sightedness; reading glasses; hearing normal by his report</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

