    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Burning pain, numbness and tingling in the fingers of both hands, brought on by cold for many winters and worse this winter, with the fingers turning white then blue then red in the cold; average pain 6 of 10; cause not yet established at intake; nerve conduction studies and neurology consultation requested</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R20.2</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented frostbite of the fingers; superseded by the diagnosis at the neurology consultation.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Cold-induced neuropathic pain and cold sensitivity of the fingers of both hands, a late sequela of frostbite in early adulthood: small-fiber pattern with normal nerve conduction studies, cold allodynia and reduced pinprick at the fingertips, and cold-induced vasospasm</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M79.2</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the neurology consultation, linked to his documented frostbite of the fingers.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Old fracture of the upper end of the right humerus, set at sea and rehabilitated without surgery: forward flexion and abduction limited to about 120 degrees, without pain at rest</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>S42.201S</td><td>S — Synthetic modern coding of his documented shoulder fracture; the range of movement is synthetic.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

